# NCBI dbGaP analysis accession:	pha004766
# Name:	COPD-affection
# Description:	Genome-wide association meta-analysis; included the COPDGene study, the UK Biobank, and the following ICGC cohorts: ARIC - Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, Cardiovascular Health Study (African and European ancestries), ECLIPSE - Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points, EOCOPD and ICGN - Boston Early-Onset COPD Study and International COPD Genetics Network, Lung Expression Quantitative Trait Loci Study, Framingham Heart Study, KARE - Korean Association Resource project, Transcontinental COPD Genetics Study, Korea, Lifelines, Lovelace, MESA - Multi-Ethnic Study of Atherosclerosis (African, European, and Hispanic ancestries), NETT/NAS - National Emphysema Treatment Trial / Normative Aging Study, GenKOLS - Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort, Transcontinental COPD Genetics Study, Poland, Rotterdam Study (1, 2 and 3), and SPIROMICS - Subpopulations and intermediate outcome measures in COPD study.
# Method:	Logistic regression, with COPD as outcome, was performed in individual cohorts, checked for orientation and hg19 chr and positions. Summary statistics for each cohort were further assessed using EasyQC. Then, a fixed-effects meta-analysis was performed using METAL. Variants from the meta-analysis were only further examined if they were present in the UK Biobank as well as at least 11 ICGC studies.
# Human genome build:	38
# dbSNP build:	141

# SNP ID:	Marker accession
# P-value:	testing p-value
# Chr ID:	chromosome
# Chr Position:	chromosome position
# ss2rs:	ss to rs orientation.  +: same; -: opposite strand.
# rs2genome:	Orientation of rs flanking sequence to reference genome.  +: same orientation, -: opposite.
# Allele1:	genomic allele 1
# Allele2:	genomic allele 2
# pHWE:	p-value from HWE testing
# &beta;:	Absolute value of regression coefficient
# SE:	Standard error of coefficient
# Coded Allele:	coding allele


